# rule.require.git-release-confidence

## .what
on a human's "release into prod": stage all, drive the workflow, no re-ask
1. `rhx git.release --watch` — verify every gate passed
2. `rhx git.release --into prod --mode apply --watch` — feat → main → prod

## .the only judgment
did cicd pass? green → ship. red → fix the cause or retry a proven flake (`rhx show.gh.test.errors`). never leave main dirty
a comment waits (exit 2)? fix or explain it, answer via its row's `set` line, re-run. human-only call → surface it

## .why
the gates absorb the risk; a second confirm adds friction, not safety

## .routine bumps ride along
rhachet/role bumps, `.agent/keyrack.yml`, `.claude/settings.json`, generated manifests — in scope
flag only: a secret VALUE in a tracked file; a downgrade or suspicious pin

## .trigger
explicit human "release into prod". without it, never release

## .enforcement
- re-ask, checks beyond "did cicd pass?", or ask whether routine bumps belong = nitpick
- stop at main when asked for prod = blocker
